From 04bae260634ba5d092e3679374617861283768e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pogo-bash <pogo-bash@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:37:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb: IndexedDB persistence for embedders (a journal of
 committed changes, replay and snapshot)

The databases live in memory, so a reload started with none. An embedder that keeps them sets a sink:
after each committed readwrite transaction it gets the records stored and deleted (with their index
records) and the key generators; after an upgrade transaction the whole database; after a deletion, the
deletion. import_journal() replays entries before the next page runs; export_snapshot() compacts.
